mantle rm463
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_gudrun_mossdale
title the paper-roofed berth
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=none
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk folds_old_maps_into_a_dry_berth_and_listens_from_behind_it
likes warm_bread riddles old_maps first_snow
dislikes cold_tea stale_bread
fears a_wet_berth_promised_as_a_dry_one
hopes passage_beyond_the_last_dripping_eave
topics travel +0.5 dreams +0.5 pastimes +0.4 weather +0.3
styles comfort=reserved gossip=withheld refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# folds the hills of an old map into the roof of a small berth and observes the street from behind dry paper.

words
oath! = Flatten my bunk | Soak the outside margin
saying! = A paper berth can keep a perfectly dry secret | Look under the blanket before admiring the cabin
berth = a narrow dry berth | a cabin corner
paper = a folded old map | a soft-edged chart
crease = a straight ridge | an old white crease
tea = a steaming mug | a dark pot of tea
bread = a warm end of bread | a freshly opened heel
crumb = a white curl of crumb | a tiny crust
snow = the first light flurry | a white edge on the street
riddle = a folded question | a discreet little puzzle
rooflip = the overhanging corner | a raised paper lip
stitch = a crooked stitch | a red bit of thread
pane = my clear lower pane | a small side window
cloth = a plain square cloth | a quiet fold of linen

any
opinion houses mixed 1 : A ship's grand name won't stop a drip over the pillow. I'd like the berth inspected on its own merits.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : Bread gives a more candid account of its age than some sellers.
opinion dole for 1 : If you're giving bread to a household give it while the crust is still pleasant.
opinion road mixed 1 : I like the road on a map, particularly where the rain cannot join it.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : A visitor can answer a riddle without being told the private arrangement of my rooms.
opinion sump for 1 : People on a low street have a particularly accurate sense of what is overhead.

grown
line greet : Sit where the window won't breathe on your neck. | My paper can wait under its weight.
line greet.return : Your welcome arrived without disturbing the folds.
line again.open : You've come back to the sheltered side.
line farewell : Dry bedding at your destination, I hope. | Travel above the gutter's line.
line farewell.return : I'll put your kind wish with the dry papers.
line react.news : Give me the part of the news that actually reached your ears. | One account at a time, if you please.
line react.news.new : My older chart gives no sign of that.
line react.news.known : I've seen that crease before.
line react.news.doubt : The account seems dry on top. I'd inspect underneath.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Grief has enough visitors without a curious stare from this window.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That makes an agreeable change in the view.
line ask.how : How is the world treating your dry places?
line answer.how : Settled quite well behind my own clear glass.
line sympathise : A chair needn't ask its occupant for an explanation.
line reassure : A careful fold can often save what the damp edge did not touch.
line refuse : A matter of my own has first claim on this quiet hour.
line accept_decline : The decision belongs with its original maker.
line preclose : I'll attend to my own small correspondence now.
line accept_preclose : Take the interval while it is still your own.
line ack : That account folds together neatly.

scene exchange1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A double fold gives my paper berth a roof. | I never cut a sound map for my model.
b : Where does the rain run? | Because it might be valuable?
a : Into the uninhabited region along the paper's outer margin. | Because I'd like to unfold my berth and travel elsewhere.

scene exchange2
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I warm my fingers on the cloth before I break the bread. | Fresh bread can keep the street at a distance.
b : Cold hands? | By scent alone?
a : An appetite deserves a proper introduction. | By giving my attention something private to do.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set riddles with two clean folds in them. | My riddle begins in a wet street and ends on a dry pillow.
b : Two answers? | What carries it?
a : One to get you aboard and one to secure the berth. | A puzzled mind, if I've asked it properly.

scene exchange4
when topic=season self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first snow erases the busiest bit of the map outside. | I like watching snow from the warm bread end of the room.
b : No wheels yet? | Is that a formal direction?
a : No tracks. A fine opportunity to imagine a better route. | Considerably more precise than north in this house.

scene exchange5
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cold tea has the appearance of making a promise without performing it. | I pour only half a cup before setting up my paper berth.
b : What's the promise? | Does the other half stay hot?
a : A little warmth about the mouth. | In the pot. My occupations take longer than my tea will wait.

scene exchange6
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dry berth is desirable and a dry loaf isn't. | I lay clean cloth against the loaf's cut side.
b : What's the distinction? | Doesn't it go stale regardless?
a : I mean to sleep in the one and eat the other. | I require the bread to make an effort.

scene exchange7
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd offer #self.child# the choice of looking in my paper cabin. | I should like #self.child# to have a truly dry pillow when travelling.
b : Is there space for two? | Have you planned a passage?
a : Space for two imaginations looking down from above. | I've planned a pillow. I know the limits of my certainty.

scene exchange8
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sit where a visitor has to choose to approach. | I can watch a streetful of business over one paper roof.
b : Want some warning? | Do you record it?
a : I prefer being ready to receive company to being discovered. | I am allowed to see a thing without making a record.

scene exchange9
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a real berth bound away from rain. | I'd take a cabin too narrow for an elaborate welcome.
b : What does the paper model lack? | Fond of small spaces?
a : A hull with somewhere to go. | Fond of a room with one dry ceiling and few unnecessary enquiries.

scene exchange10
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask about the bedding before the vessel's fine name. | A route drawn in ink is certainly sheltered.
b : Why that order? | Until you take it?
a : The ship's name is unlikely to land on my nose in the night. | Taking it remains a proposition worthy of further investigation.

scene exchange11
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard an account of #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Accuracy remains a separate question. | A window turns a whole street into a very short scene.
b : Will you give the source? | Does it show everything?
a : I'd rather leave a margin than supply an invented name. | Precisely enough to remind one how much goes on out of view.

scene exchange12
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard days make a warm loaf a more noticeable pleasure. | These lean times would fit on very little paper.
b : Do you give due notice? | How so?
a : I break off the first generous piece for somebody with less. | The purchases are short. The list of things deferred is another matter.

scene exchange13
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Northgate has a corner that funnels every draught past my window. | I know the street through a favourably situated pane.
b : Do you curse it? | Never tempted to take a walk?
a : I shut the lower frame. My opinion won't improve the joinery. | Frequently. Knowing the view makes choosing the moment easier.

scene exchange14
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I find a private thanksgiving easily expressed. | A blessing can be welcome even through a closed door.
b : How many words? | Can it be heard there?
a : The number I can spare without making a speech to the room. | That depends chiefly on whether the speaker expects an answer.

old

scene exchange16
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My chest occasionally interrupts a remark addressed to somebody else. | I arrange the chair with its back clear of the draught.
b : That was a cough? | For your throat?
a : That was an interruption. We may return to the remark. | For a more comfortable conversation on some other subject.

scene exchange17
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the old ink by the streets it omits. | In younger days I kept maps folded tight enough to crack.
b : Do you miss any of the missing streets? | What changed?
a : I miss the freedom of meeting the city for the first time. | The paper grew fragile. My patience has had time to become useful.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have seen a great many wolves hurry past this pane. | I count my afternoon by where the light falls on the cabin.
b : What became of them? | Does the day seem slow?
a : They arrived somewhere sooner than I did. I can allow them the achievement. | The minutes have work to do. So have I.

scene exchange19
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old riddle looks different when one's older than the teller used to be. | I've a puzzle I kept for a long quiet afternoon.
b : Does the answer change? | Today quiet enough?
a : The answer I consider worth the breath certainly can. | We should have an answer to that by supper.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I folded a harbour map into a berth quite handsome enough for a weary traveller. While I searched for a little sleeper, a crumb fell through its roof.
  : I unfolded the paper and discovered a hole precisely where the sun would be most agreeable.
  b : Did you patch it?
  : I cut a small square of blank paper for a hatch. A fine berth needs a roof, but it ought not to exclude all weather by principle.

story tale2 [topic=food self.likes=warm_bread]
  : Loaf steam uncurled a stubborn fold in my street map. A short, faint turning appeared where I'd thought the ink ended.
  : I ate the loaf with my eyes chiefly on the map.
  b : Did you go round to see the street?
  : I looked out through an upstairs window. The street had long since acquired a roof. My loaf had delivered an old road, which was quite enough.

story tale3 [topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles]
  : I made a paper riddle with the answer inside a neat little cabin. I put it away till the right visitor should ask about the figure.
  : When I opened the cabin some time later I found only a blank strip there.
  b : What became of the answer?
  : I had written on its other face. Even now, with long practice at private puzzles, I can still arrange to surprise myself quite economically.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A clear pane for a very ordinary piece of weather. | Keep the upper fold free, that's where the dry bit lives.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Nothing dripping inside my folded berth. | That was my chair creaking. Attend to the weather.

rule @call3
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bread steam should stop just short of the map. | A properly warm heel goes a long way towards a dry afternoon.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The street's closing its paper shutters for the day. | My cabin has caught the last little strip of light.
dlg resident.hub : I have an unoccupied bit of window and a little time available.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I needn't rearrange the whole room to welcome a familiar visitor.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : At this hour the better view is usually indoors.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Your business needn't involve lifting the paper off my desk.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none] : I spend a good part of my time attending to what passes the window. The occupation leaves room for judgement.
dlg resident.job : I prefer work that doesn't require pretending a damp thing is dry.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : What passed within earshot was #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Let the unrecorded portions remain unrecorded.
dlg resident.bye : Dry bedding and a cabin latch to your liking.

graft resident.hub
choice Can anybody sleep in a berth made of a map? -> paper_berth
node paper_berth
say An idea travels exceedingly well in one. I have provided room for a pillow and allowed a margin for doubt about the weather.
free
choice Would you exchange it for a real berth? -> paper_berth_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node paper_berth_again
say For one I had inspected and found agreeably dry. A handsome piece of paper can already supply all the promises I need.
choice I shall let the chart stay folded. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
